WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
 If you really stop and think about it, walking into a modern hospital is just this profound

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.280
 act of trust.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.280
 Oh, absolutely.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.960
 But there's this underlying expectation you carry through those sliding glass doors.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.360
 It's an expectation of absolute mechanical control.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.360
 Right.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.000
 It feels like walking into a factory that is designed exclusively for healing.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.840
 Going with a broken part, they will you into this brightly lit, totally sterile room.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.680
 The doctors fix the part and you go home.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.720
 Yeah, it feels predictable, feels safe.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.440
 We really want to believe that medicine is just, you know, a series of highly scheduled,

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.320
 perfectly executed protocols.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.880
 And I mean, in a lot of ways it is.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.480
 But the reality is that human physiology doesn't read the textbook.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.600
 No, it definitely does not.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.400
 Your body, my body, anyone listening to this right now, our bodies are these incredibly

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.240
 complex, sometimes entirely unpredictable ecosystems.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.240
 Right.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.920
 And the systems we've built to care for human bodies are just constantly dancing on this

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.760
 razor thin edge.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:12.520
 It's a balance between absolute control and utter chaos, which is exactly what we are

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.520
 getting into today.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.040
 Yes, we are.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.200
 Our mission for this deep dive is to take you on a massive, really comprehensive journey

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.120
 through the incredibly high stakes world of acute, critical and transitional nursing

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.120
 care.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.280
 And we've been looking forward to this one.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:32.080
 We've spent weeks pouring over a huge stack of clinical texts, nursing protocols, and

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.000
 medical research.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.520
 And well, we are going to walk you through how the health care system categorizes, manages,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.760
 and ultimately responds to your physical vulnerability.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.200
 And we're looking at a pretty huge narrative arc here.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.200
 Yeah, massive.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.480
 We're going to start with what you might call a planned crisis, which is essentially

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.160
 what a scheduled surgery in an operating room is.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.160
 Right.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:59.240
 Physical trauma, then we are going to look at what happens when that control just vanishes

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.080
 and we move to unplanned individual crises in the ER.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.080
 The emergency department.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.080
 Yeah.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:10.360
 From there, we'll scale up to the unthinkable, which is systemic crises, like disasters,

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.360
 mass casualty events.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.360
 They're really heavy stuff.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.360
 Yeah.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.360
 And finally, we'll explore those profound, quiet moments when medical intervention reaches

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:23.120
 its absolute limits, shifting into palliative and end of life care.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.680
 It's a vast spectrum of care, for sure.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.320
 But you know, if you keep an ear out, you'll hear a connecting thread throughout this entire

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.320
 discussion.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.320
 What's that?

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.720
 It's the clinical judgment and the rigid, sometimes brutal protocols that keep the whole

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:41.360
 medical system from just collapsing when human bodies are at their absolute most vulnerable.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.600
 And I promise you, there are some truly fascinating, just mind blowing extremes we are going to

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:47.600
 unpack today.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.600
 Oh, absolutely.

