00:42:22.280 --> 00:42:23.640
 The foundation of it all.

00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:26.880
 This is the absolute core foundation of emergency management.

00:42:26.880 --> 00:42:30.800
 It is a strict algorithm designed to find and fix the specific things that will kill

00:42:30.800 --> 00:42:34.440
 the patient the fastest in the exact order they will kill them.

00:42:34.440 --> 00:42:36.600
 It follows the ABCDE method.

00:42:36.600 --> 00:42:39.640
 Airway, breathing, circulation, disability, and exposure.

00:42:39.640 --> 00:42:40.640
 Right.

00:42:40.640 --> 00:42:42.120
 And the sequence is non-negotiable.

00:42:42.120 --> 00:42:45.920
 You do not worry about a shattered femur if the patient's airway is blocked.

00:42:45.920 --> 00:42:46.920
 Never.

00:42:46.920 --> 00:42:47.920
 A is airway.

00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:48.920
 Are they choking?

00:42:48.920 --> 00:42:50.720
 Is there blood or vomit in the throat?

00:42:50.720 --> 00:42:52.720
 Establish patent C immediately.

00:42:52.720 --> 00:42:53.720
 And B?

00:42:53.720 --> 00:42:58.000
 B is breathing, the airway might be open, but are the lungs actually functioning?

00:42:58.000 --> 00:42:59.440
